    "sections": {
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the <code>letterhead</code> folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory, or install from the WordPress Plugin Repository.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in your WordPress Network Settings.</li>\n<li>Once activated, navigate to &#8216;Network Admin&#8217; <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> &#8216;Settings&#8217; <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> &#8216;Letterhead&#8217; to configure the plugin.</li>\n<li>Enter your Letterhead API key and map your sites to their respective Letterhead channels.</li>\n<li>Save your settings. Your posts will now be curated to Letterhead based on your configuration</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>0.2.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>✍️ Updated the readme changelog order and updated the version.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>0.2.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>You can now map a single site to many channels 💃.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>0.1.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Adds logos for our WordPress Plugin page.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>0.1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release. 🥳</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "description": "<p>Connect each site in a WordPress Multisite to its Letterhead channel to automatically curate posts.</p>\n"
    },
